The City reported, among others, the following significant accomplishments in CY 2023:
a. Continued mass vaccination at various vaccination centers within the City;
b. Kalinga sa Manila Project to six districts of Manila;
c. Distribution of monetary assistance to families affected by multiple fire incidents;
d. Distribution of Christmas food boxes to six districts of Manila;
e. Construction/ repair/ rehabilitation/ improvement/ upgrading/ installation of various structures and facilities:
Completion of the following major infrastructure projects:
1. Construction of Manila Science High School;
2. Installations of Solar Studs (Phase 3);
Ongoing construction of the following projects:
1. Installation of traffic signal lanterns at various street intersections in the City;
2. Construction of Dr. Albert Elementary School;
3. Construction of Rosauro Almario Elementary School;
4. Construction of San Sebastian Residences;
5. Construction of Pedro Gil Residences;
6. Construction of San Lazaro Residences;
7. Construction of 10-storey, 232 classrooms school building at Ramon Magsaysay High School;
8. Installation of solar road studs (Phase 4);
9. Construction of six-storey School Building at Emilio Jacinto Elementary School; and
10. Construction of six-storey School Building at Aurora A. Quezon Elementary School.
In the same year, the City received the 2023 I-ACT Magiting na Lingkod Award.

The significant observations and recommendations that need immediate action are as follows:
1. Insufficient imposition of Real Property Tax and Special Education Tax by the City due to: a) Misplaced application of the Assessment Levels (ALs) prescribed under Section 12 of Ordinance No. 8331, s. 2013; and b) Omission of 1,130 Real Property Units (RPUs) in the Assessment Rolls (AR) contrary to Section 2, Chapter II, Manual on Real Property Appraisal and Assessment Operations, thereby diminishing the City’s earnings to be utilized to finance its programs/projects/activities.
We recommended and the Management agreed that:
a. The Office of the City Assessor –
Ensure that Assessment Levels and Assessed Values are accurately computed and provided;
Submit to the Auditor’s Office the updated copies of Tax Declaration as proof of corrections/updates made to the 452 RPUs;
Appraise and assess the RPUs not included in the Assessment Roll and submit copies of tax declaration as proof appraisal and assessment;
Review other tax maps not included in the sample to ensure that RPUs inscribed therein are included in the AR;
Henceforth, ascertain that RPUs in the tax maps are included in the AR; and
b. The CTO charge and collect from taxpayers the amount of P3,336,539.51 that were under imposed in CY 2023 due to erroneous application of the Assessment Level, and henceforth, ensure that correct amount of taxes is imposed/collected.
2. A total of P472.416 million withheld for CY 2023 remittances to the BIR, GSIS, Pag-IBIG and PhilHealth have not been remitted by the City contrary to existing rules and regulations.
We recommended and Management agreed to ensure prompt and full remittance of all withholding taxes, contributions, premium payments, loan amortization and other amounts due to the BIR, GSIS, Pag-IBIG and PhilHealth pursuant to the above-mentioned regulations.
The aforementioned observations together with the corresponding recommendations were discussed with Management officials concerned during the exit conference on April 30, 2024. Management views and comments were incorporated in the report, where appropriate.
